usb: gadget: f_ncm, f_rndis: forget os_desc_table at unbind

ncm_unbind() and rndis_unbind() free f->os_desc_table but keep the pointer, and the next bind allocates a new
table only when the gadget uses OS descriptors (cdev->use_os_string, from configfs os_desc/use). A gadget bound
with os_desc/use=1, unbound, bound with use=0 and unbound again frees the same 16-byte table twice.
mu300-adbd does exactly that on every restart (adb out of the gadget: use=0; adb back in: use=1), and the
kernel has no SLAB_FREELIST_HARDENED to stop it: on 2026-10-22 the kmalloc-16 freelist came back as "-lan",
the tail of the kernfs link name "upper_br-lan" written into the twice-freed table, and kstrdup() in
gadget_dev_desc_UDC_store() oopsed on it. Mainline 7.3 has the same two lines, so this is for every kernel.

--- a/drivers/usb/gadget/function/f_ncm.c
+++ b/drivers/usb/gadget/function/f_ncm.c
@@ -1749,6 +1749,7 @@
 	hrtimer_cancel(&ncm->task_timer);

 	kfree(f->os_desc_table);
+	f->os_desc_table = NULL;
 	f->os_desc_n = 0;

 	ncm_string_defs[0].id = 0;
--- a/drivers/usb/gadget/function/f_rndis.c
+++ b/drivers/usb/gadget/function/f_rndis.c
@@ -949,6 +949,7 @@
 	rndis_opts = container_of(f->fi, struct f_rndis_opts, func_inst);

 	kfree(f->os_desc_table);
+	f->os_desc_table = NULL;
 	f->os_desc_n = 0;
 	usb_free_all_descriptors(f);
